MARC MARON'S ADVENTRES IN MOVIEGOING ️ In the latest episode of our Criterion Channel original series the fearlessly unfiltered comedian and cultural commentator joins “The Ringer”’s Sean Fennessey for a discussion of his relationship to cinema, from childhood exposures to highly age-inappropriate films to his obsession with silent-movie stars to his evolving relationship with the French New Wave. Alongside their conversation, introduces a selection of art-house touchstones by Michelangelo Antonioni (RED DESERT), Wim Wenders (THE AMERICAN FRIEND), and Rainer Werner Fassbinder (VERONIKA VOSS), auteurs whose films he views as puzzles that continue to inspire questions and fascination even after multiple viewings.<p><img src="https://prank-arum.github.io/Feeds/Instagram/marcmaron/6731221625123167565251.jpg"><p><a href="https://pixnoy.com/post/6731221625123167565251">Original post on Picnob</a>]]>
